          "option_id": "052d3ba5-d650-4718-90b3-b0c76f5243c4",
          "text": "Overwhelming early- life events",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "option_id": "caa804ac-7dda-4b3c-a834-1ecf59ed69d3",
          "text": "Self- mutilation",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "option_id": "f64a4171-04b2-479f-b53f-4b539b44cbee",
          "text": "Low levels of hypnotic capacity",
          "is_correct": true
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": {
        "letter": "D",
        "option_id": "f64a4171-04b2-479f-b53f-4b539b44cbee",
        "text": "Low levels of hypnotic capacity"
      },
      "correct_answers": [
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "option_id": "f64a4171-04b2-479f-b53f-4b539b44cbee",
          "text": "Low levels of hypnotic capacity",
          "is_correct": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "ANSWER: D Individuals with dissociative identity disorder often have multiple types of interpersonal maltreatment, including overwhelming early-life events such as medical illness. Self-mutilation and suicidal behavior are also common. These individuals usually have greater hypnotic capacity and dissociativity, not lower.",
      "explanation_images": [],
      "explanation_image_url": null
    },
    {
      "question_number": 8,
      "question_id": "6b440fa3-23bd-401a-a514-97337f1cef12",
      "question_type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
      "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
      "question_text": "The type of amnesia MOST common in dissociative amnesia is:",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "image_url": "",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "option_id": "74653279-0194-48ec-bf39-58e39498898e",
          "text": "Localized amnesia",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "option_id": "a6a88580-902c-4e52-ae92-c2e700abd076",
          "text": "Selective amnesia",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "option_id": "0f078a92-5878-4f6b-b319-ea9c1a03bd6e",
          "text": "Generalized amnesia",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "option_id": "62b978b3-dc5a-467d-811b-8f01e5dc047f",
          "text": "Systematized amnesia",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": {
        "letter": "A",
        "option_id": "74653279-0194-48ec-bf39-58e39498898e",
        "text": "Localized amnesia"
      },
      "correct_answers": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "option_id": "74653279-0194-48ec-bf39-58e39498898e",
          "text": "Localized amnesia",
          "is_correct": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "ANSWER: A The most common form of dissociative amnesia is localized amnesia, a failure to recall events during a specific period of time. Selective amnesia is when the individual can recall some, but not all, of the events during a period of time. Generalized amnesia is a complete loss of memory for one's life history. Systematized amnesia is a loss of a specific category of information.",
      "explanation_images": [],
      "explanation_image_url": null
    },
    {
      "question_number": 9,
      "question_id": "e49257f5-73d9-47e4-ab8b-abcd39e0791c",
      "question_type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
